Bennett-Wiesner dense coding: Alice sends the two bits 1 1 by applying
Z then X (Z = p p, X = h p p h) to her half (qubit 0) of an EPR pair.
Bob decodes with CNOT then H and reads both bits determinately.
Outcome: m 0 gives the Z bit (1), m 1 gives the X bit (1).
